UNTESTED ON A PHONE. Host check: check-01-shim.sh.
What: removes smmu_check_ufs() from the shim. The check walks SMRs until it finds stream 0x60, and the hypervisor aborts
reads of SMR 7, so any boot where ABL leaves the stream later or nowhere ends in the red exception screen with no reason
about UFS. A translating mapping is still caught: the START STOP UNIT or READ DMA below fails and the shim prints why.
Apply: cd ios-sweet && git apply ../plans/boot/01-shim-drop-smmu-check.patch

diff --git a/asteroids/shim/ufs.c b/asteroids/shim/ufs.c
index 952efed..be42e21 100644
--- a/asteroids/shim/ufs.c
+++ b/asteroids/shim/ufs.c
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
